<% content_for(:html_title, 'Trust — EsignCenter') %>
<% content_for(:html_description, 'Where your data lives, who processes it, and the evidence behind every claim EsignCenter makes: recorded consent, sealed and timestamped PDFs, public verification, open source.') %>
<% content_for(:canonical_url, trust_url) %>
<% content_for(:indexable, 'true') %>
<%# The trust page (Session 9). Every row of the claim register was checked against the code it cites before it was written; the ERB comment beside each row names the file. If a row stops being true, fix the product or delete the row — never soften the wording. %>

<section class="mk-ground">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-2 pt-14 pb-12 md:pt-20 md:pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-700">Trust</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">What we claim, and the proof</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg md:text-xl text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">This page says where your data lives, who else touches it, and what stands behind each promise on our site. Every claim points at code you can read. Where we cannot prove something, we do not say it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-2 py-12 md:py-16" aria-labelledby="where-heading">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-4">
      <h2 id="where-heading" class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Where your data lives</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4 text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
      <%# The SOC 2 Type II reports are the hosting and storage providers' own (Render and AWS, named on /trust/subprocessors), not EsignCenter's; the #not-claimed paragraph says so. %>
      <p data-soc2 class="font-semibold text-base-content">Built on SOC 2 Type II audited infrastructure.</p>
      <p>The application, the database that holds your account, templates and audit events, and the documents you upload and sign all live in United States regions. The services we use, and what each one receives, are on our <%= link_to 'sub-processors page', subprocessors_path, class: 'link font-medium' %>.</p>
      <p>You can take everything with you at any time: <strong>Settings → Export</strong> builds one zip of your account with a manifest of checksums, and <strong>Settings → Account</strong> lets an administrator delete the account, confirmed with their password or a code we email them. Deletion is a 90-day decision: the account goes read-only immediately, and on the date shown it is permanently destroyed, unless you cancel before then.</p>
      <p>A few things outlive a permanent deletion, on purpose: the verification record of each signed PDF (its SHA-256 fingerprint, completion date and signer count, kept permanently so a document can still be verified years later; it holds no names and nothing from the document), the subscription and payment history with the person scrubbed out of it, a stub of the account row so those records point at something, and our own log of support access to the account. A file that another account also uses stays for that account. Everything else is destroyed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-2 py-12 md:py-16" aria-labelledby="register-heading">
  <h2 id="register-heading" class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">The claim register</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-base-content/70 max-w-2xl">Every promise our site makes, with the evidence behind it in plain English. The <a href="<%= Docuseal::GITHUB_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link">source code</a> is public, so each one can be checked.</p>
  <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-white">
    <table class="block md:table w-full text-left text-base">
      <caption class="sr-only">Claim register: each marketing claim and the evidence for it</caption>
      <thead class="hidden md:table-header-group bg-base-200/70 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-base-content/70">
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="px-4 md:px-6 py-3 font-semibold md:w-1/3">We say</th>
          <th scope="col" class="px-4 md:px-6 py-3 font-semibold">What stands behind it</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="block md:table-row-group">
        <%# lib/esign_consent.rb (sender-attested API completions exempt by design), lib/submission_events.rb (create_with_tracking_data), lib/submissions/generate_audit_trail.rb (consent row) %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="consent">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">Signer consent is recorded</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">Everyone who signs on our signing pages must first tick "I agree to use electronic records and signatures". That tick is stored as a versioned consent event with the date and time, the signer's IP address, the language the notice was shown in and the SHA-256 fingerprint of the exact disclosure text, and it is printed in the audit trail. The one deliberate exception: a document a sender marks as already completed through the API has no human signer on our pages, so no consent is collected or claimed for it; the audit trail shows it as sender-attested instead.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# lib/submissions/generate_result_attachments.rb (build_signing_params), lib/submissions/timestamp_handler.rb, lib/platform_certificate.rb, docs/operations.md (TIMESERVER_URL) %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="sealed">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">Signed PDFs are sealed and timestamped</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">Every completed PDF carries a PKCS#7 digital signature made with the EsignCenter platform certificate and an RFC 3161 timestamp from DigiCert's public timestamp authority. If the timestamp service cannot be reached the signing job fails and retries; it never embeds a local clock instead. Change one byte of the file afterwards and the seal no longer checks out.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# app/controllers/verify_controller.rb, app/models/verified_document.rb, docs/verify.md %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="verify">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">Anyone can verify a document</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">The <%= link_to 'verify page', verify_path, class: 'link' %> needs no account. It checks the file's SHA-256 fingerprint against the record we keep of every PDF we sign, a record that survives account deletion, and confirms our signature on the file. It answers only with the completion date and the number of signers. Names, email addresses and document contents are never shown.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# lib/submissions/generate_audit_trail.rb (events: send_email, view_form, complete_form, esign_consent, IP line) %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="audit">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">A full audit trail comes with every document</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">A PDF audit trail is generated with each completed document. It lists, in order and with timestamps, when the document was sent, opened, agreed to and signed, by which signer, from which IP address, and includes the verification each signer passed.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# config/storage.yml (S3, AWS_REGION default us-east-1), docs/render-deploy-checklist.md, docs/operations.md %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="us">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">Your data is stored in the United States</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">The application, database and files all run in US regions. The providers are listed on the <%= link_to 'sub-processors page', subprocessors_path, class: 'link' %>.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# lib/accounts/export_archive.rb (manifest.json with per-file SHA-256), app/controllers/account_exports_controller.rb, docs/account-deletion.md %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="export">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">You can export everything</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">Settings → Export builds one zip with your templates, documents, signed PDFs, audit trails and CSV records, plus a manifest listing every file with its size and SHA-256 checksum. Anything that could not be included is named in the manifest rather than silently left out.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# app/controllers/accounts_controller.rb, lib/accounts/deletion_codes.rb (emailed code), lib/accounts/purge.rb + docs/account-deletion.md "What survives a purge" (verified_documents, account_subscriptions, scrubbed stripe_event_inboxes, the tombstone row; operator_events untouched) %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="delete">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">You can delete your account yourself</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">An administrator can delete the account from Settings → Account, confirmed with their password or an emailed code. The subscription is cancelled at once, the account goes read-only, every administrator is emailed the date, and 90 days later everything is destroyed except the records listed under "Where your data lives" above. Any administrator can cancel the deletion before then.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# lib/docuseal.rb (GITHUB_URL), LICENSE, app/views/shared/_powered_by.html.erb (AGPL attribution) %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="open-source">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">Open source</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">EsignCenter is a fork of DocuSeal. The complete source, including everything on this page, is public under the AGPL at <a href="<%= Docuseal::GITHUB_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link break-all"><%= Docuseal::GITHUB_URL %></a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# app/mailers/account_mailer.rb (support_access_started), app/views/accounts/_support_access.html.erb (SupportImpersonation.recent_for), lib/support_impersonation.rb + app/controllers/concerns/support_impersonation_guard.rb (impersonation.start/.end/.action/.refused rows), app/views/shared/_support_impersonation_banner.html.erb %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="support">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">Support access is visible</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">When our support opens a session inside your account, your administrators are emailed at once with the reason, and every session appears in a "Support access" card on your Settings → Account page with who, when, how long, and what changed. Every change the session makes, and every door it is refused at, is logged; the person on our side sees a bright banner the whole time. Support sessions cannot touch billing, passwords, API keys or anything irreversible.</td>
        </tr>
        <%# lib/quotas/limits.rb, lib/entitlements.rb, lib/pricing_matrix.rb (load-time coverage check) %>
        <tr class="block md:table-row border-t border-base-content/5 align-top py-3 md:py-0" data-claim="pricing">
          <th scope="row" class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-2 pb-1 md:py-4 font-semibold">The pricing page tells the truth</th>
          <td class="block md:table-cell px-4 md:px-6 pt-1 pb-2 md:py-4 text-base-content/80">The comparison table on the <%= link_to 'pricing page', pricing_path, class: 'link' %> is generated from the same constants the product enforces. The test suite fails if a paid feature is ever gated in the app without appearing in the table.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-base-200/50 border-y border-base-content/5" aria-labelledby="not-heading">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-2 py-12 md:py-16 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-4">
      <h2 id="not-heading" class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">What we do not claim</h2>
    </div>
    <div id="not-claimed" class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4 text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
      <p>EsignCenter itself holds no certifications. The SOC 2 Type II reports behind our infrastructure belong to our hosting and storage providers, not to us: we have no SOC 2 report of our own, no HIPAA assessment, and we do not offer a data processing agreement. If your work needs those, EsignCenter is not the right tool yet, and we would rather say so here than in a sales call.</p>
      <p>Nothing on this site is legal advice. Whether an electronically signed document is enforceable depends on the document, the law that applies to it and the people involved; what we can promise is the evidence above, kept accurately, for every document you sign here.</p>
      <%# Both doors on purpose: the support form routes it and gets a receipt, and the raw address stays visible because a security report must not depend on a form, a CAPTCHA or JavaScript working. %>
      <p>Found a security problem? <%= link_to 'Tell us on the support form', support_path, class: 'link font-medium' %> (choose "Security report"), or email <%= mail_to Docuseal::SUPPORT_EMAIL, Docuseal::SUPPORT_EMAIL, class: 'link font-medium' %> directly. A real person reads it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-2 py-16 text-center">
  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Check a document</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-base-content/70 max-w-xl mx-auto">Upload any PDF and learn whether it was completed through EsignCenter, when, and by how many signers.</p>
  <%= link_to 'Verify a document', verify_path, class: 'mt-6 btn btn-neutral text-white btn-lg text-base px-8' %>
</section>
